% nav-belief step 2 fixture (spec/16 §10.1, rows by TICK): opus's world-model cycle. A tick opens at stage robot
% (the robot's one event, a step or a wait, and the beasts' wake), then stage beasts (one engage-or-hold per beast
% still free). The beasts' first-passage hazards come by tick in nina's predict_table shape: closing(B, I) per row,
% I the beast's intent, a categorical belief. `fuel` and `ticked` are the fixture's: fuel ends the world (for
% metispy's witness), and ticked counts the ticks it reads the rows by.
catalog crossing 1.
provenance hand "a crossing with two beasts: rows by tick" "2026-10-26".
layers (dyn).
stages (robot beasts).
type cell {c0 c1 c2 c3 c4}.
type beast {b1 b2}.
type intent {hostile wandering}.
namespace cr produce (dyn).
pred at(cell) : cr.
pred turn : cr.
pred free(beast) : cr.
pred held(beast) : cr.
pred engaged(beast) : cr.
pred intent(beast, intent) : cr.
pred home : cr.
pred fuel : cr.
pred ticked : cr.
bwd next(cell, cell).
next(c0, c1).
next(c1, c2).
next(c2, c3).
next(c3, c4).
bwd stairs(cell).
stairs(c4).
weight mind(B, I) reads {intent(B, I)}.
weight closing(B, I) reads {intent(B, I)}.
stage robot {
  %% I step on from {P} to {Q}.
  walk [dyn] : turn * at(P) * next(P, Q) -o at(Q)  @w 0.7.
  %% I wait at {P}.
  wait [dyn] : turn * $at(P) -o ()  @w 0.3.
  %% {B} is free again.
  wake [dyn] : held(B) -o free(B).
  %% At the stairs.
  arrive [dyn] : at(P) * $stairs(P) -o home.
}
%% The robot has moved: the beasts' turn.
qui to_beasts [dyn] : robot -o beasts.
stage beasts {
  %% {B}, {I}, engages me.
  engage [dyn] : free(B) * $intent(B, I) -o engaged(B)  @w closing(B, I).
  %% {B}, {I}, holds off this tick.
  hold [dyn] : free(B) * $intent(B, I) -o held(B)  @w ~closing(B, I).
}
%% The beasts have moved: the next tick opens at the robot.
qui to_robot [dyn] : beasts * fuel -o robot * turn * ticked.
#init at(c0) 1
#init turn 1
#init free(b1) 1
#init free(b2) 1
#init fuel 10
#belief intent one I by mind
#port mind(b1, hostile) 0.5
#port mind(b1, wandering) 0.5
#port mind(b2, hostile) 0.2
#port mind(b2, wandering) 0.8
#port closing(b1, hostile) step 0.3 0.5 0.7
#port closing(b1, wandering) step 0.05 0.05 0.1
#port closing(b2, hostile) step 0.2 0.4 0.6
#port closing(b2, wandering) step 0.02 0.02 0.05
#evaluate engaged risk engaged(_) within 3 tick robot
#evaluate stairs reach home within 4 tick robot
#evaluate engaged_at risk engaged(_) at 3 tick robot
